Logos
-----
A row leads with the logo of the machine, the program or the format its file
is from (app/src/main/res/drawable/logo_*.xml). The logos are trademarks of
their owners, used here only to say what a file is; nothing about them is
licensed under the GPL, and their use implies no endorsement. Each was taken
from Wikimedia Commons (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:<name>), cut
to what it draws and resized; five were also redrawn with their black in
white for dark themes (logo_*_dark.xml). As Commons has them:

Public domain (too simple to be copyrightable; trademarked):
    Commodore 64 logo-5.svg, NES logo.svg, Super Famicom logo.svg,
    Gameboy logo.svg, Gameboy advance logo.svg, Nintendo DS Logo.svg,
    Nintendo 64 wordmark.svg, Playstation logo colour.svg,
    MegaDriveJPLogo.svg, SEGA logo.svg, PC engine logo red.svg,
    MSX-Logo.svg, Atari logo.svg, Sinclair ZX Spectrum-01.svg,
    PC9800 logo 1982.svg, Commodore Amiga US Logo.svg, Ad Lib logo.svg,
    FLAC logo vector.svg, Mp3.svg, Ogg Logo.svg, Opus logo2.svg,
    Apple Lossless logo.svg, WavPack logo.svg.

CC0 1.0:
    Nintendo GameCube symbol logo.svg.

Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/):
    AAC Logo.svg - see its page on Commons for its author.

